From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:10:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 53/55] hottyterm: a secondary press on an element that takes
 it is the surface's (SPEC 9)

A secondary press on a surface is the surface's where an element there or
outward has secondary in its data-on (hotty_host_secondary, HOST.md 3), as
a left click on one is. hotty-blitz decides; hottyterm only asks.

- Surface.mouseButtonCallback's existing hook (Hotty.surfaceButton) asks
  for a .right press over a surface that takes the pointer, with device
  pixels from the surface's top left and the mods as the pointer hook
  passes them. When it answers true the press is consumed: no mouse report,
  no right-click-action (no word selection, context menu or paste), and
  Ghostty's state of the button goes back to released. The matching release
  is consumed too, remembered in Hotty.secondary_down.
- When it answers false nothing changes: Shift gives Ghostty's menu
  (mouse-shift-capture), Alt with mouse reporting on gives the program's
  report (SGR button 2 plus Alt's 8), otherwise right-click-action. Plain
  moves still go to hotty as hover.
- Not asked while a press on the cells holds the pointer.

Upstream files: 0 lines added (the existing hook calls in).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
